## CAA Policy

**Found at:** example.com

| Flags | Tag | Value |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | issue | letsencrypt.org |
| 0 | issuewild | pki.goog |
| 128 | iodef | mailto:security@example.com |

**iodef (incident reporting):** mailto:security@example.com

**Wildcard:** issuewild permits CA(s) not allowed by issue (pki.goog) — wildcard issuance is broader than named issuance

> CAA is checked by CAs at issuance time, not by clients at validation time. A cert whose issuer is not in the current CAA policy is not invalid — it may have been issued before the policy was set, or under a parent zone. Treat mismatches as informational.
